<title>SINGAPORE: TIBS Holdings plunges to 1st-half loss.</title>
<headline>TIBS Holdings plunges to 1st-half loss.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net loss				1.59   vs   3.41 (gain)</p>
<p>    Loss per share (LPS) (cts)	3.50   vs   7.50 (gain)</p>
<p>    LPS fully-diluted basis (cts)   1.30   vs   6.40 (gain)</p>
<p>    Turnover			     77.36   vs  63.43</p>
<p>    Other income incl interest	0.99   vs   1.82</p>
<p>    Interest expense		    1.28   vs   0.62</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortization	13.50   vs   6.80</p>
<p>    Income from associates	    0.10   vs   0.11</p>
<p>    Pre-tax loss			  1.98   vs   5.15 (gain)</p>
<p>    Tax				     0.53   vs   1.87</p>
<p>    Minority Interests		  0.83   vs   0.03</p>
<p>    Extraordinary item		   nil   vs   0.72 (loss)</p>
<p>Note - TIBS Holdings Ltd a diversified bus and taxi company with investments in machine-related products and services.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
